</span></span></strong></p>
<div>
<div>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">To the Public Records =
Advocate / Attorney General's Office:</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">&nbsp;</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">I filed a Petition for=
 Review of Denial of Public Records Request in this matter on July 22, 2026=
, and a first supplemental on July 24, 2026. I write to supplement the reco=
rd a second time.</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">&nbsp;</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">On July 27, 2026, five=
 days after the petition was filed, Oregon State Police notified me that a =
thorough review has identified additional responsive records and that it is=
 reopening PR27478, with production
 estimated at three weeks. I do not withdraw the petition. The Department's=
 notice resolves none of its counts =97 it describes no search, cites no ex=
emption, rules on no fee waiver, and does not say whether the recorded disp=
atch communications for March 24,
 2026 still exist.</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">&nbsp;</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">The attached supplemen=
tal filing places the Department's own admission in the record; identifies =
the one assertion in it that cannot be correct as written (that records of =
a March 24 event were &quot;not in our system&quot;
 on April 3); and renews, with urgency, the single time-sensitive request i=
n this matter =97 whether the March 24 dispatch recordings still exist and =
whether any responsive record has been destroyed, purged, or allowed to age=
 off a retention schedule since April
 2, 2026. That question can be answered in a sentence and does not depend o=
n the three-week review now underway.</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">&nbsp;</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">The filing is attached=
, together with the newly added exhibits: Exhibit 27 (the Department's reop=
ening notice) and Exhibit 28 (my response of July 27, 2026). Exhibit 26 (th=
e July 24, 2026 letter from the District
 Ranger) was filed with the first supplemental and is included in the attac=
hed package for reference.</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">&nbsp;</span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"color:black">Respectfully,</span></=
